Author:     John Bieling <john@thunderbird.net>
AuthorDate: Tue Jan 14 22:44:59 2025 +0000
Commit:     John Bieling <john@thunderbird.net>
CommitDate: Tue Jan 14 22:44:59 2025 +0000

    Bug 1933970 - Enforce generic extension icon at root level, if no icon specified in manifest. r=Paenglab,micahilbery

    Extension icons in context menus are not only used to identify *which*
    extension an entry belongs to (the icon at root level cannot be changed,
    it is always the extension icon which is also shown in the add-on
    manager), but also to indicate that the entry is in fact an extension
    entry.

    If an extension did not define an extension icon in its manifest,
    the entry currently looks like an standard entry from Thunderbird
    itself.

    By enforcing the generic extension icon (which is also used in the
    add-on manager), we not only make it obvious to the user, that the
    entry is from an extension, but we also fix all the remaining
    alignment issues.

    This change is in line with other WebExtension components, which
    fallback to the generic extension icon, for example our action buttons.

    The bugzilla bug itself has a reproducer add-on, to verify the actual
    issue in an unpatched Thunderbird, and the fixed alignment after
    applying the patch.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D232791

diff --git a/mail/components/extensions/parent/ext-menus.js b/mail/components/extensions/parent/ext-menus.js
index a00ab4a8c09..68e07988318 100644
--- a/mail/components/extensions/parent/ext-menus.js
+++ b/mail/components/extensions/parent/ext-menus.js
@@ -263,17 +263,18 @@ var gMenuBuilder = {

     if (forceManifestIcons) {
       for (const rootElement of children) {
-        // Display the extension icon on the root element.
-        if (
-          root.extension.manifest.icons &&
-          rootElement.getAttribute("type") !== "checkbox"
-        ) {
+        // Display the extension icon on the root element. Fallback to the generic
+        // extension icon, if there is no extension icon specified in the manifest.
+        if (rootElement.getAttribute("type") !== "checkbox") {
           this.setMenuItemIcon(
             rootElement,
             root.extension,
             contextData,
-            root.extension.manifest.icons
+            root.extension.manifest.icons || {
+              16: "chrome://messenger/content/extension.svg",
+            }
           );
+          rootElement.classList.add("webextension-rootElement");
         } else {
           this.removeMenuItemIcon(rootElement);
         }
diff --git a/mail/themes/shared/mail/contextMenu.css b/mail/themes/shared/mail/contextMenu.css
index 070d775e64e..deef24fa25e 100644
--- a/mail/themes/shared/mail/contextMenu.css
+++ b/mail/themes/shared/mail/contextMenu.css
@@ -128,7 +128,7 @@ menupopup {
   }

   /* Allways show the extension icons. */
-  &.no-icon-menupopup > :is(menu, menuitem)[image^="moz-extension"] > .menu-iconic-left {
+  &.no-icon-menupopup > :is(menu, menuitem).webextension-rootElement > .menu-iconic-left {
     display: flex;
   }
 }
